@AGENTS.md

## Claude Code skills

Project-specific Claude skills live in `.claude/skills/`; Claude Code loads them when the work matches. Detailed conventions are documented there.

- `spring-boot-conventions` - module structure, layers, controller/service/DTO patterns
- `backend-feature-delivery` - contract-first backend feature delivery across OpenAPI, DTOs, services, persistence, and schema changes
- `observability-and-telemetry` - logs, metrics, traces, Actuator exposure, and async context-propagation guidance
- `authorization-rules` - method security, ownership checks, and business-policy access rules
- `external-integrations-and-resilience` - timeouts, retries, idempotency, remote error translation, and transaction boundaries around external systems
- `auditing-and-actor-context` - entity timestamps, actor attribution, and domain audit trail guidance
- `performance-and-query-shaping` - query authoring, fetch strategy, specifications, pagination, and N+1 review expectations
- `caching-strategy` - cache suitability, TTL, invalidation, and local versus shared cache tradeoffs
- `migration-conventions` - Flyway naming, SQL style, and database migration conventions
- `jackson-spring-boot4` - Jackson 3.x split namespace, ObjectMapper injection
- `jpa-kotlin-patterns` - entity patterns, AuditableEntity, relationships, N+1 prevention
- `error-handling` - ApiException, GlobalExceptionHandler, error codes
- `security-auth` - JWT, endpoint security, OAuth2, public vs authenticated
- `testing-patterns` - JUnit Jupiter 6, MockK, unit vs integration test conventions
- `test-endpoint` - generate curl and Postman requests for manual endpoint checks; complements `testing-patterns`
- `deployment` - worked examples for deploying the backend container (Azure Container Apps); the user and their agent own the cloud choice, the secrets and the deployment

## Backend Claude Commands

- `/add-endpoint` - add or evolve a backend API endpoint using the OpenAPI-first flow
- `/create-migration` - create a Flyway migration for schema work
- `/add-integration` - add a typed outbound or callback integration with resilience rules
- `/document-entity` - create or update backend entity documentation
- `/generate-clients` - regenerate API clients from the shared contract
- `/review-query` - review fetch plans, pagination, specifications, and N+1 risk
- `/review-security-surface` - review route exposure, token handling, and authorization boundaries
- `/debug-prod-issue` - guide production issue diagnosis across logs, metrics, traces, config, and migrations
